<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoParseInfix</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>function to parse infix-notation expressions</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/ParseInfix.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoNode *SilikoParseInfix(SilikoLexer *lexer);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoParseInfix</function> function parses
the Siliko infix language from tokens supplied by
<varname>lexer</varname>. <function>SilikoParseInfix</function>
generates a syntax tree of <type>SilikoNode</type> objects representing
the parsed input. The
parser takes ownership of <varname>lexer</varname>, and will call
<function>SilikoLexerDestroy</function> on it when finished.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Value</title>
<para><function>SilikoParseInfix</function> returns a pointer to the
root node of the syntax tree generated from parsing the input from the
input source or <literal>NULL</literal> if it is unable to allocate
memory.</para>
</refsection>
</refentry>
